    explain: "### Jazz melodic minor\nThe *ascending* melodic minor used in both directions: **1 2 b3 4 5 6 7**, a major scale with a minor 3rd. It's the minor tonic with a leading tone (mMaj7, m6), and its modes give most of the 'jazz' chord-scales.\n\n### CAGED shapes for any scale\nA CAGED shape is a region of the neck anchored on a chord shape's roots: E and G shapes on string 6, C and A shapes on string 5, D on string 4. Any 7-note scale fills that region with a 2–3 notes-per-string fingering. You already know these for major. For other scales, keep the **roots where they are** and move only the degrees that change: melodic minor lowers each 3rd by a fret, harmonic minor lowers each 3rd and 6th.\n\n| mode | formula | chord |\n|---|---|---|\n| Melodic minor | 1 2 b3 4 5 6 7 | mMaj7, m6 |\n| Dorian b2 | 1 b2 b3 4 5 6 b7 | sus4(b9) |\n| Lydian augmented | 1 2 3 #4 #5 6 7 | maj7#5 |\n| Lydian dominant | 1 2 3 #4 5 6 b7 | 7#11 |\n| Mixolydian b6 | 1 2 3 4 5 b6 b7 | 7b13 |\n| Locrian nat2 | 1 2 b3 4 b5 b6 b7 | m7b5(9) |\n| Altered | 1 b9 #9 3 #11 b13 b7 | 7alt |\n\n### Melodic minor modes: origin and use\n| mode | parent: degree | one note away | played over | where you meet it |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Melodic minor | melodic minor, 1st | Dorian (7→b7), Ionian (b3→3), harmonic minor (6→b6) | mMaj7, m6 | the minor tonic, e.g. the i at the end of a minor ii–V–i |\n| Dorian b2 | melodic minor, 2nd | Dorian (b2→2), Phrygian (6→b6) | sus4(b9) | the sus(b9) chords of modal jazz; Phrygian-type vamps |\n| Lydian augmented | melodic minor, 3rd | Lydian (#5→5) | maj7#5 | the bIII+ of a minor key; a brighter stand-in for Imaj7 |\n| Lydian dominant | melodic minor, 4th | Mixolydian (#4→4), Lydian (b7→7) | 7#11 | dominants that don't resolve down a 5th: IV7 in a blues, bVII7, the tritone sub bII7 → I |\n| Mixolydian b6 | melodic minor, 5th | Mixolydian (b6→6), Aeolian (3→b3) | 7b13 | the V7 of a minor key when you want a natural 9 |\n| Locrian nat2 | melodic minor, 6th | Locrian (2→b2), Aeolian (b5→5) | m7b5 (natural 9) | the iiø7 of a minor ii–V–i |\n| Altered | melodic minor, 7th | Locrian (b4→4), altered diminished (b7→bb7) | 7alt | the V7alt that resolves to I or i: maximum tension before the resolution |",
