    explain: "The fastest way to learn a scale that you only half know: one string, whole length, saying the degrees. Then the scale is a *sound and a step pattern*, not a fingering.\n\n### Melodic minor modes: origin and use\n| mode | parent: degree | one note away | played over | where you meet it |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Melodic minor | melodic minor, 1st | Dorian (7→b7), Ionian (b3→3), harmonic minor (6→b6) | mMaj7, m6 | the minor tonic, e.g. the i at the end of a minor ii–V–i |\n| Dorian b2 | melodic minor, 2nd | Dorian (b2→2), Phrygian (6→b6) | sus4(b9) | the sus(b9) chords of modal jazz; Phrygian-type vamps |\n| Lydian augmented | melodic minor, 3rd | Lydian (#5→5) | maj7#5 | the bIII+ of a minor key; a brighter stand-in for Imaj7 |\n| Lydian dominant | melodic minor, 4th | Mixolydian (#4→4), Lydian (b7→7) | 7#11 | dominants that don't resolve down a 5th: IV7 in a blues, bVII7, the tritone sub bII7 → I |\n| Mixolydian b6 | melodic minor, 5th | Mixolydian (b6→6), Aeolian (3→b3) | 7b13 | the V7 of a minor key when you want a natural 9 |\n| Locrian nat2 | melodic minor, 6th | Locrian (2→b2), Aeolian (b5→5) | m7b5 (natural 9) | the iiø7 of a minor ii–V–i |\n| Altered | melodic minor, 7th | Locrian (b4→4), altered diminished (b7→bb7) | 7alt | the V7alt that resolves to I or i: maximum tension before the resolution |\n\n### Harmonic minor modes: origin and use\n| mode | parent: degree | one note away | played over | where you meet it |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Harmonic minor | harmonic minor, 1st | Aeolian (7→b7), melodic minor (b6→6), harmonic major (b3→3) | mMaj7, m(b6) | the minor tonic with a leading tone: classical and minor-key melodies |\n| Locrian nat6 | harmonic minor, 2nd | Locrian (6→b6) | m7b5 (natural 13) | the iiø7 of a minor ii–V–i |\n| Ionian #5 | harmonic minor, 3rd | Ionian (#5→5) | maj7#5 | the bIII+ of a minor key; a rare colour |\n| Dorian #4 | harmonic minor, 4th | Dorian (#4→4) | m7(#11) | the iv of a minor key; 'Ukrainian Dorian' in klezmer and Eastern European folk |\n| Phrygian dominant | harmonic minor, 5th | Phrygian (3→b3), Mixolydian b6 (b2→2) | 7(b9 b13) | the V7 of a minor key (E7 → Am); flamenco, klezmer, metal |\n| Lydian #2 | harmonic minor, 6th | Lydian (#2→2) | maj7(#9 #11) | the bVImaj7 of a minor key; an exotic major colour |\n| Altered diminished | harmonic minor, 7th | altered (bb7→b7) | dim7 | the vii°7 that leads back to the minor tonic |",
